49. We have examined the FIR, charge sheet, examination-in-chief, cross-examination, exhibits and other documents in the record. We have also carefully perused the judgment passed by the trial Court in the light of submissions of all parties.&nbsp; 

 50. Now let us analyse the depositions made by the witnesses. PW 1, Jiban Krishna Roy, Deputy Director, Anti-Corruption Commission in his examination-in-chief stated that he was authorized to investigate into the FIR case of the accused appellant and on investigation he found 6 FDRs being Fixed Deposit Account Nos. 00175018437 Taka 22 lakh, 001755018442 Taka 20 lakh, 001755018582 Taka 9 lakh, 00155018558 Taka 26 lakh, 001755018566 Taka 20 lakh, 00175501574 Taka 20 lakh totaling into Taka 1.17 wore were deposited during the period between 17-4-2006 to 17-4-2007 with IFIC Bank, Karwan Bazar, Dhaka; that Dr. Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir was served with a notice from Anti-Corruption Commission under Memo dated 18-2-2007 to submit statement of movable and immovable properties; that the notice was served upon the accused appellant to the Central Jail Part-1, Kashsimpur, Gazipur and he submitted statement in his own hand writing to the Anti-Corruption Commission through Jail Super Notice was served upon the accused appellant on 18-2-2007 and he received the same on 20-2-2007. The notice under section 26 of the said Act is Exhibit 1. Notice was issued by Secretary of Anti-Corruption Commission, Delwar Husain. The Statement of Assets given by the accused appellant included a forwarding report which are Exhibit 2 series attested by the Jailor. The Statement of Assets as given by the accused appellant was forwarded through Jail Super, Part I, Kashimpur. Forwarding letter is Exhibit 3. On getting the statement, the Secretary of the Commission asked PW 1 to investigate into the statement of assets and accordingly, be submitted his report after examination with the Commission on 4-3-2007. Permission was accorded to lodge the FIR against the appellant on 6-3-2007. The sanction letter is Exhibit 4 After investigation and examination of the Statement of the Assets he then lodged the Ejahar. He in his chief further stated that in the statement of assets and in the income tax return of the appellant there is no mention of Fixed Deposit kept in Karwan Bazar IFIC. Bank worth Taka 1.17 crore and also he did not show any source of that amount. He stated that the appellant acquired huge wealth beyond his known source of income and thereby committed offence under sections 26 and 27 of the Anti-Corruption Act, 5(2) of the Prevention of Corruption Act, 1947, Emergency Power Rules 15(Ka)(Kha) Ga(5), 2007 and section 409 of the Penal Code and therefore lodged the FIR which is Exhibit 5. He stated that SI Md Idris on 6-3-2007 filled up the FIR which is Exhibit 6. In cross-examination, he stated that he investigated into the matter pursuant to the direction of the Anti-Corruption Commission. He investigated into the matter for 11 days, i.e. from 22-2-2007 to 4-3-2007. On inquiry he found that the appellant is a political personality. During investigation he did not go to the residence at Banani along with others but he went there on 10-2-2007 along with 4 other members of the task force team. He denied that he went to the house as per direction of the Secretary of Anti-Corruption Commission. He stated that he sub-sequent read the notice under section 26 of the said Act i.e. Exhibit. He conceded that the said notice did not ask the appellant to mention the valuation of the property. The said notice also did not require the appellant to mention the properties belonging to others. He conceded that he investigated into the properties in Kachua, Chandpur and came to know that the properties are ejmali properties. He admitted that out of 6 FDRs, 2 FDRs were to be matured on 17-4-2007 and the rest on 18-4-2007. He confessed that the tax was to be deducted on 30-6-2007. He confessed that he in the FIR did not specifically state as to the time and place when and where the appellant acquired any property by abusing of power. He further confessed that he did not make any investigation on Item 4 of the Statement of Assets. He also stated that he has no knowledge as to whether all family members of the appellant contributed in Sultana Foundation, a proposed Family Trust. He confessed that he did not get any allegation of corruption against the appellant and also he did not make any investigation on that. He stated that FDR is not a confidential matter and the government deducts tax on the interest of FDR on its maturity. He conceded that there was no gazette notification for appointment of the Investigating Officer. He confessed that he did not investigate the bank account, FDR. It was stated by PW 1 that Mrs. Setara Begum, wife of Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir, is aged about 60 years and she was a teacher and she is not dependent on the accused. Elder son Dr Jalal Alamgir is in a teaching profession in the USA and his yearly income is 12 thousand dollars which is equal to Taka 84 lakh and he is not dependent on the appellant. Younger son of the appellant is Dr Joy Alamgir, a graduate from Cornell University in USA and his yearly income is 13,000 Dollars equal to Taka 91 lakh. He is aged about 28 years and he is not dependent upon the accused appellant. There are 13 publications of the accused and he received Taka 20,000 as royalty. Exhibit 3 is the letter asking the appellant to submit property statement of Setara Alamgir, wife of Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. In Exhibit 4 there is no direction of the Commission to lodge Ejahar. So the record speaks that there is a violation of section 32(1) of the said Act. The record further speaks that them is an approval for submitting charge sheet but there is no sanction of the said Commission to take cognizance of the case by Special Judge. He did not find any account either current or savings with the IFIC Bank of the appellant. As per procedure of the bank, the Tax Department makes statement of interest after its maturity and then inform the NBR. He admitted that the appellant mentioned source of income in his statement of property.&nbsp; 

 52. PW 3 is AMM Aminul Haque, First Vice-President and Manager, IFIC Bank, Karwan Bazar Branch, Dhaka. In his examination-in-chief he stated that on 25-3-2007 Deputy Director Zibon Krishna Roy of Anti-Corruption Commission went to his office and he seized 6 FDRs of Dr. Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. The FDR or Fixed Deposit were kept against current Account Nos. 001755018434 dated 17-4-2006 of Taka 22,00,000, FDR No. 001755018442 dated 17-4-2006 of Taka 20,00,000, FDR No. 001755018558 dated 18-4-2006, FDR No. 001755018574 dated 18-4-2006 Taka 20,00,000, FDR No. 001755018582 dated 18-4-2006 Taka 9,00,000, FDR No. 001755018582 dated 18-4-2006 Taka 20,00,000, FDR No. 001755018566 dated 18-4-2006 Taka 20,00,000, totalling Taka 1,17,00,000. All these FDRs matured after one year. Zibon Krishna Roy, Inspector examined all those FDRs, FDR Vouchers and initial signature cards and seized the same and kept in his Zimma. He signed in the seizure list which is Exhibit 7. He deposited 6 FDR application forms, initial signature cards, Fixed Deposit Register original copy, and thereafter submitted photocopy of those papers before the Court which is Exhibit 8. Photocopy of issue register is Exhibit 10. In his cross-examination he stated that those 6 FDRs of the accused will come to its maturity on 17-4-2007 and 18-4-2007. There is 10% deduction of tax on FDR. The interest and excise duty were sent to the NBR. Six FDRs were not kept in secret which are recorded in the bank. Those six FDRs were not kept secret to NBR. Interest was deducted during tax assessment year 2007-2008. It was not possible on his part to say whether the six FDRs belong to Sultana Foundation. He stated that FDR is Amanat.&nbsp; 

 54. PW 5 AFM Shoeb, First Assistant Vice-President, IFIC Bank, Karwan Bazar Branch, Dhaka, in his examination-in-chief stated that on 25-3-2007 while he was working in the bank the Deputy Director of Anti-Corruption Commission went to the bank and in his presence seized six FDRs Register, Voucher, initial signature board which are Exhibit 7 that were seized and kept with the bank Manager. FDRs were also produced before the Court. In both voucher and FDR he put his signature and in other four FDRs ex-Manager Shahid Atiqul Islam signed. In his cross-examination, he met with the informant Zibon Krishna Roy 2/3 times. He does not know Sharmin Ferdousi. No one recorded his statement. He denied that on 17-4-2006 Sharmin Ferdousi recorded his statement. Further, he stated that Amanat is called financial instrument IFIC Bank has financial instrument.&nbsp; 

 57. PW 8 Nasrin Ara Surat Amin is the Director (Investigation) of Anti-Corruption Commission. In her examination-in-chief, she stated that she was assigned to get the property statement of Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir under Memo dated 18-2-2007 and the notice contained the signature of the Secretary. On 21-2-2007 the Property Statement was sent from Kashimpur, Gazipur through his brother Dr Borhan Uddin Khan Jahangir and he came on 22-2-2007 and deposited the same to him. The signature is Exhibit 3/1. The Statement is Exhibit 2 and it was placed before the Secretary and then it was marked for investigation which is Exhibit 3. After investigation the informant Zibon Krishna Roy submitted his report and Anti-Corruption Commission approved him to lodge the FIR. The letter is Exhibit 4. In her cross-examination, she stated that there is no direction in the notice requiring the appellant to mention as to valuation of the movable and immovable property. He denied that the Secretary is not authorized to serve notice on behalf of the Commission. She did not submit any proceeding nor any complaint lodged by anybody. She did not file any paper that any one authorized her to serve notice upon Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. She also did not submit any proceeding before the Court. She further denied that she did not examine any complaint.&nbsp; 

 58. PW 9 is CMA Matin, Senior Jail Super, Kashimpur Central Jail, Part-I, Gazipur. In his examination-in-chief stated that on 20-2-2007 Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir was in custody in Central Jail, Kashimpur, Gazipur. He received the notice dated 18-2-2007 of Anti-Corruption Commission and notice was served upon Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir on 20-2-2007, He has prepared the Property Statement on 20-2-2007 and that was sent to the Jail authority on 21-2-2007. The property statement of 20-2-2007 is kept with judicial record. The report was handed over to the wife of Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. He signed the forwarding report which is Exhibit 3. Accused Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir was a detainee in Kashimpur Jail. He denied that he did not sign any letter, notice or any paper while he was under detention. On 21-2-2007 it was a holiday. Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir submitted in his Property Statement for the first time on 21-2-2007. Forwarding is Exhibit 2. Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir submitted his report with the jail office. He further denied that he was not given 72 hours but only 2/3 hours was provided for submission of the statement.&nbsp; 

 62. PW 13 Sufi Md Abul Hasnat, Sub-Divisional Engineer in his examination-in-chief stated that at the direction of the Executive Engineer of PWD he went to Chandpur, Kachua to ascertain the valuation of the property of Setara Bhaban, Sultana Filling Station, Biponi Palash along with A Rab and Md Zakir Hossain, Assistant Engineer on 8-4-2007. At the time of measurement of the Filling Station, the Manager was present. As per the drawing and the persons and from the information of the persons present the valuation of the Biponi Palash was assessed. The assessment report is Exhibit 13 series. From the plinth area of Setara Bhaban, the expense thereof was determined and then he submitted report to Executive Engineer, Chandpur. In cross-examination, he stated that before going to Kachua he did not take SP Chandpur with them. He could not remember the name of the Union where he had gone. He did not ask for any Union Parishad Chairman or Ward Member to accompany them nor he saw any name as &quot;AI Ashek Falak&quot; in the nameplate affixed on the said building. He gave statement to the Investigating Officer on 12-5-2007. He made his statement sitting in the Chamber of Executive Engineer, Shologhar, Chandpur from 11-30 AM to 12-30 PM. He further stated that he went to the Filling Station along with SI and Constable. After seeing drawing of the constructed building the construction expenses was determined and he could not remember whether he stated to the Investigating Officer to that effect. He did not mention the Mouza and Khatian number. He could not say any name of elites of that area. He did not mention the employees of the said building. They did not take any Surveyor. Further he stated that they could not enter into the house nor could they enter into the room. They did not take any measurement. He could not state what materials were fitted in the railing and in the stepping nor could he say as to how many rooms were in the ground floor. On measurement of the plinth area report was submitted. The number of rooms, kitchen, bath-room were not determined. The age of the boundary wall was not ascertained. He admitted that they did not make any hole in the building nor did they inspect the record to determine whether the building belonged to Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. Therefore the valuation made by them has no weight.&nbsp; 

 63. PW 14 Md Abdur Rab, also Sub-Assistant Engineer, in his examination in chief stated that they went for determination of construction expenses, namely Sultana-Setara Bhaban, Sultana Filling Station, Biponi Polash as per direction of Executive Engineer of Public Works Department of Chandpur. He along with Sub-Divisional Engineer and Sub-Assistant Engineer went to Kachua on 8-4-2007. He took the measurement of Sultana Filling Station first in the sequence and then went to the building at Gulbahar. They took rough measurement of those two houses prepared by his Assistant. Then they went to the Biponi Potash an under construction building near the Cold Storage and took the measurement by taking the map and after determining The valuation of the construction the same was placed with the Executive Engineer which is Exhibit 14 series. In his cross-examination he stated that while taking the measurement there were four members. In the rough measurement there is no file number nor there is any letter of reference and them is no page number of measurement. All measurement entries must be in the measurement book. The rough measurement book is not in the office. There are some pencil or ink marks in the rough measurement but there is no initial mark. For determination of the valuation he did not consult site plan, architecture plan, planning plan, electrical plan. The rate of construction of PWD is same. He has no knowledge that the house was constructed at the time of his father. There are articles for measurement of building materials. He has no knowledge about the quality of the products. It is not known to him that the house belongs to four brothers and four sisters of Dr. Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. He denied that the Sultana Filling Station belongs to Dr. Jalal Alamgir, son of Dr. Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. He also did not know that Gulbahar Cold Storage and Biponi Potash do not belong to personal assets of the appellant or those are the assets of a private limited company. He could not remember that the rough measurement was written sitting at Chandpur. It appears that PW 14 gave his evidence on the basis of rough measurement which does not carry any weight.&nbsp; 

 65. PW 16 Md Helal Ahmed, Sub-Divisional Engineer, in his examination-in-chief stated that in the report he put his signifier which is Exhibit 15. He took the valuation of the property situated under Kotwali Police Station of Housing Estate at section 1, Block N, Plot No. 8 and while he went for valuation, the Executive Engineer, Sub-Assistant Engineer were not present. In presence of Executive Engineer he took measurement and submitted report to the Executive Engineer. In his cross-examination, he stated that he started measurement on 5-4-2007 and completed on the same date. It was computer composed on 3-5-2007. But the person who computerized such report, his name is absent in the report. There is no signature in the report on each page.&nbsp; 

 68. PW 19, Md Nasim, Sub-Divisional Engineer, Sher-e-Bangla Nagar, PWD. Sub-Division 5, Dhaka, in his examination-in-chief stated that for the purpose of valuation of the property situated at Banani Road No. 25, House No. 16 a committee was formed. Member of the committee went thereon and took the measurement. The accused Dr. Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir on 19-4-2007 sent a letter in which it is stated that the first and second floor was constructed in the year 1981-82 and third and fourth floor in the year 1991-92 and they made the valuation of the property on measurement. They valued the said building at Taka 86,28,562. The civil construction expenses, electrical expenses and sanitary expenses were annexed with the valuation. They took measurement on 8-4-2007 and on that very date it was completed. They have not received any map or any documents while they had taken the measurement. He did not ask for any paper from Dr. Borhan Uddin Khan Jahangir. He did not make any contact with RAJUK for determination of the year of construction. He did not consider the expenses on the point of salary of the worker for the year 1981-82 and 1991-92. It can&#39;t be understood how much cement and rod were used by reading the report. The valuation of the brick, sand and other materials also could not be determined from the report. Mr. Karim submits that on the evidence given by PW 19 the valuation report of PW 19 had no basis.&nbsp; 

 69. PW 20 Md Mostafa, Assistant Engineer, Sher-e-Bangla Nagar, Sub-Division-5, Dhaka went to Banani for taking measurement upon the direction of the Deputy Director Zibon Krishna Roy, Anti-Corruption Commission. In his examination-in-chief he stated that there was a committee constituted by five members and he is one of the member, He went to take measurement for determination of the construction valuation. First and second floors was constructed in the year 1981-82 and third, fourth and fifth floors were constructed in the year 1991-92 and the construction valuation was taken on the basis of civil construction and the expenses comes to Taka 50,82,947, electric valuation expenses Taka 14,45,615 and total valuation comes to Taka 86,28,562. In cross-examinant he stated that he passed Diploma from Khulna Polytechnic Institute in the year 1994-95, the post was non-gazetted. He has no education on survey. He has no knowledge for taking measurement. He has taken about 17 days in preparation of the report and it was prepared sitting in the office. The report was forwarded to Jibon Krishna. He submits that he is not a credible witness and his evidence does not carry any weight.&nbsp; 

 70. PW 21 Mahbubul Hoque Chowdhury, Sub-Divisional Engineer in his examination-in-chief stated that he went to take the valuation of the property situated at Banani on the direction of Chief Engineer. They took the measurement and prepared the report and he has given the electric portion in the report. In cross-examination, he states that in the committee he is the only electrical expert. He did not see electrical designs of the house. He did not follow the design of electricity of the building. From the report it cannot be ascertained how much electrical goods were used in the 5th floor of the building and also there is no means to ascertain as to how much electrical goods were utilised in the 4th, 3rd, 2nd and 1st floors and the ground floor. The measurement Part C was done jointly and that has been determined as per present market valuation and valuation of those parts comes to Taka 24,45,615. He denied that the report was prepared sitting in the office. We have examined Exhibit 16 on the basis of which the valuation of Banani house was determined. While determining the value the rates were taken as of the market rates. The Banani building was constructed in the year 1981-82 whereas rates were adopted for the year 2006. The rate for the year 2006 can be made applicable for the construction of building erected in the year 1981-82. The valuation of Banani house as assessed is without any basis and has no evidentiary weight.&nbsp; 

 76. PW 27 is Santi Ranjan Baidhya, Head Assistant, District Registrar Office, Chandpur. In his examination-in-chief he stated that on 12-5-2007 the investigating officer prepared the seizure list and he signed in the seizure list. He seized some papers from the District Registrar Office.&nbsp; 

 77. PW 28 is AKM Fazle Hossain Assistant Inspector, Anti-Corruption Commission, Dhaka. In his examination-in-chief stated that the seizure list was prepared by the Deputy Director Syed Iqbal Hossain who is the investigating officer. He seized and prepared seizure list. Receipt of three motorcycles and some papers as to acquisition of the property were seized and the seizure list is Exhibit 20. In cross-examination, he stated that the papers relating to acquisition does not contain any signature. Further, in cross-examination, he stated that from Exhibit 20 the ownership of motorcycles cannot be ascertained.&nbsp; 

 79. PW 30 is Md Masudur Rahman, Manager, Sultana Filling Station, Kachua, Chandpur. In his examination-in-chief, he stated that the Filling Station has no bank account. In case of necessity at the very beginning the cheques were deposited in the account of Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir and also withdrawn on that account. Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir has bank account with Janata Bank, Kachua branch. For determination of the valuation and measurement of the Sultana Filling Station a team there and another person went to Gulbahar. A seizure list was prepared and he counter-signed. In the seizure list papers relating to purchase of the Motor Cycle and of Sultana Filling Station and the land acquisition for the Filling Station were seized and he signed in that seizure list. Sultana Filling Station belongs to private owner and the owner is Dr Jalal Alamgir, living in America. All the papers relating to the Filling Station belong to Dr Jalal Alamgir. Since Dr Jalal Alamgir likes abroad, thus the account is maintained in the account of Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. At the beginning, some cheques and Demand Drafts were deposited in the account of the appellant. He himself deposits and withdraws all the money of the said Filling Station. In case of necessity, money was withdrawn from the account of Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir through pay order and after that it was returned to Han and all those transactions are informed to Dr Jalal Alamgir.&nbsp; 

 81. PW 32 is Bashra Haron Debnath, Manager, Bangladesh Krishi Bank Gulbahar Branch, Kachua, Chandpur. He stated that Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir has a Savings account as well as Current account. The statement was given on 13-5-2007 to Syed Iqbal Hossain, Deputy Director, Anti-Corruption Commission, Head Office, Dhaka. Forwarding is Exhibit 22 and the statement is Exhibit 23. Savings Account No. 1 dated 9-5-2007 had balance of Taka 62,169/68 and Current Account No. 11 dated 9-5-2007 had balance of Taka 26,409. In cross-examination, he stated that he could not say how many current and savings account exist in his bank and he could not say the balance of his bank on 30-6-2005 and 31-12-2005. He could not remember whether the investigating officer has taken statement for that period. The statement indicated in debit balance, so the evidence given by PW 32 does not show that there was any concealment on the part of the appellant.&nbsp; 

 82. PW 33, SM Kamal Hossain, Manager, Gulbahar Cold. Storage, Palashpur, Kachua, Chandpur, stated that he was working there for 10 years. Biponi Palash is an under construction building. He stated that Gulbahar Cold Storage is a limited company and Biponi Palash is owned by the said company. He could not remember how many share-holders are there The Head Office of the Company at Dhaka used to submit its return.&nbsp; 

 83. PW 34 Md Anowar Hossain, Manager, Grameen Bank, Kadla, Kachua Branch, Chandpur, in his examination-in-chief stated that on the direction over telephone of Syed Iqbal Hossain, Deputy Director, Anti-Corruption Commission Savings account No. 100053 of accused Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir was found and its balance is Taka 11,000. The account was opened on 5-12-2006, Setara Alamgir has Savings Account No. 100045 and that was also opened on 13-9-2006. The balance amount is Taka 6,138. The report was sent to Syed Iqbal Hossain which is Exhibit 25. In his cross-examination, he could not say how much money was in the account of accused Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir.&nbsp; 

 85. PW 36 is Sharmin Ferdousi, Deputy Director (Prosecution), Anti-Corruption Commission, Head Office, Dhaka who in her examination-in-chief stated that she took over the investigation from Deputy Director Zibon Krishna Roy by an order of the Anti-Corruption Commission on 3-3-2007. She received the record and started investigation. She examined Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir and recorded his statement under section 161 of the Code of Criminal Procedure and seized the documents. Seizure list is Exhibit 11. She recorded the statement of the officer of IFIC Bank, Karwan Bazar Branch wherein six FDRs were deposited. Six FDRs were valued at Take 1.17 crow. She stated that the appellant suppressed those FDRs while giving statement with Anti-Corruption Commission and also in his income tax file during 2006-2007. She told that sanction was obtained on 29-4-2007 for submitting charge sheet. The sanction letter is Exhibit 28. Thereafter submitted charge sheet under sections 26, 27 of the Anti-Corruption AM, 2004 read with Rule 15 Ghe(5) of the Emergency Power Rules, 2007 dated 21-7-2007. Therefore she submits that the notice was sent by the Secretary Md Delwar Hossain. There is nothing in the law that the Chairman or Secretary can issue notice. From the record it appears that the Ex-Secretary appointed investigating officer for investigation and report was also submitted addressing to him. Ex-Secretary Delwar Hossain was not made witness and also he was not examined. Notice did not say to submit the valuation of the property. Income tax officer Rabiul Hassan did not say that there is any difference in the income tax file and that he made statement under section 161 of the Code of Criminal Procedure on 12-4-2007. There were three investigating officers and she could not say whether she completed the investigation within the stipulated period. From the statement of the accused it appears that the wife of the accused and his sons were self-sufficient. In case of necessity they helped the accused. The statement as to source of income is given in page No. 3, paragraph No. 4 under serial No. Ka to Fa. in paragraph No. 45 in his statement there is mention of investment in ICB and the Share in Gulbahar Cold Storage, Private Ltd Company share She denied that the FDR was not concealed and it is known to NBR. She denied that the accused meant FDR as Amanot and she could not understand that the Amanat means FDR.&nbsp; 

 88. DW 1 Dr Akbor Ali Khan in his examination in chief stated that he is known to the appellant since 1961.&nbsp;
